 down.","sources":["who-anc-sym","who-nv","unicef-t1"]},"fatigue":{"label":"Tiredness","self_care":"Rest when you can, go to bed earlier and keep eating iron-rich foods. Energy often returns in the second trimester and dips again near the end.","call_doctor_if":null,"sources":["mc-hp","mc-2t","unicef-t1"]},"breast_tenderness":{"label":"Sore, tender breasts","self_care":"A well-fitting, supportive bra can ease the soreness.","call_doctor_if":null,"sources":["mc-hp"]},"frequent_urination":{"label":"Needing to pass urine often","self_care":"This is common early and late in pregnancy. Keep drinking water during the day.","call_doctor_if":"It hurts or burns when you pass urine, which can be a sign of infection.","sources":["unicef-t1","who-anc-sym","mc-2t"]},"heartburn":{"label":"Heartburn","self_care":"Eat smaller meals, avoid lying down right after eating and limit foods that trigger it. If it does not ease, ask your doctor about an antacid.","call_doctor_if":"It does not improve with these changes.","sources":["who-anc-sym"]},"constipation":{"label":"Constipation","self_care":"Drink plenty of water and eat fibre from vegetables, fruit, nuts and whole grains. If that is not enough, ask your doctor about bran or a fibre supplement.","call_doctor_if":null,"sources":["who-anc-sym","unicef-t1"]},"back_pain":{"label":"Back and pelvic pain","self_care":"Regular exercise throughout pregnancy helps prevent back and pelvic pain. Physiotherapy or a support belt may also help.","call_doctor_if":"The pain comes with regular tightenings, pain when passing urine, or pelvic pain so severe you cannot walk.","sources":["who-anc-sym"]},"leg_cramps":{"label":"Leg cramps","self_care":"Stretching your calf, pulling your toes up towards you, massage, warmth and relaxation can relieve cramps. If they continue, ask your doctor whether magnesium or calcium is right for you.","call_doctor_if":null,"sources":["who-anc-sym","unicef-t1","mc-2t"]},"swelling":{"label":"Swollen feet and ankles, varicose veins","self_care":"Raise your legs when resting. Compression stockings or time in water may also help.","call_doctor_if":"Swelling is sudden or affects your face or hands, or one leg becomes painful, red or warm.","sources":["who-anc-sym","who-ds"]},"headaches":{"label":"Headaches","self_care":"Rest, drink water and keep to regular meals. Ask your doctor before taking any pain medicine.","call_doctor_if":"A headache is severe or comes with blurred vision.","sources":["unicef-t1","who-ds"]},"braxton_hicks":{"label":"Practice tightenings (Braxton Hicks)","self_care":"Irregular, painless tightenings of the belly are common later in pregnancy and usually ease with rest or a change of position.","call_doctor_if":"Tightenings become regular, painful or stronger before week 37.","sources":[]},"shortness_of_breath":{"label":"Shortness of breath","self_care":"Slow down, take breaks and sit or stand up straight to give your lungs more room.","call_doctor_if":"Breathlessness is sudden or severe, or comes with chest pain.","sources":["mc3s"]},"sleep_trouble":{"label":"Trouble sleeping","self_care":"Lie on your side with pillows supporting your belly and back. A short rest during the day can help.","call_doctor_if":null,"sources":[]},"mood_changes":{"label":"Mood changes and worry","self_care":"Mood swings and worry are common in pregnancy. Share how you feel with someone you trust and with your doctor.","call_doctor_if":"You feel sad or hopeless, or lose interest in things you used to enjoy, for two weeks or more.","sources":["mc-hp","mc-dep","owh-dep"]}},"danger_sign_labels":{"bleeding":"Bleeding","severe_headache":"Severe headache","blurred_vision":"Blurred vision","face_hand_swelling":"Swelling of the face or hands","fever":"Fever","reduced_movement":"Baby moving less than usual","leaking_fluid":"Leaking fluid or waters breaking","severe_abdominal_pain":"Severe abdominal pain"},"test_labels":{"blood_pressure":"Blood pressure check","urine_test":"Urine test","anaemia_tes