uent_urination","fatigue"],"feelings":"Feeling unwell and happy at the same time can be confusing, so be gentle with yourself.","tips":["Keep taking folic acid every day."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms","supplements"],"sources":["unicef-t1","who-anc-sym","who-ifa"],"baby":{"fact":"The neural tube, which becomes the brain and spinal cord, is forming, and early heart cells begin to pulse.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["cc","mc1"]}},{"week":6,"title":"Your Body Is Adjusting","summary":"Nausea, tender breasts and tiredness are common now. Symptoms vary a lot, and some women have very few.","symptoms":["nausea","breast_tenderness","fatigue","mood_changes"],"feelings":"Mood swings are common in early pregnancy.","tips":["Plan your first antenatal visit before week 12."],"danger_signs":["bleeding","fever","severe_abdominal_pain"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms","visits"],"sources":["unicef-t1","mc-hp","who-anc","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"The neural tube is closing and small buds that will become arms appear.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":{"kind":"image","alt":"Week 6 illustration","credit":"medicalgraphics","source_url":"https://www.medicalgraphics.de/en/product/embryo-6th-week-white/","axes":[{"id":"theme","source":"app"}],"renditions":[{"when":{"theme":"light"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-06.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":29670},{"when":{"theme":"dark"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-06-dark.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":43815}]},"sources":["mc1"]}},{"week":7,"title":"Food Cravings and Dislikes","summary":"You may crave some foods and go off others, and nausea may still be strong. Eating small amounts often can help you get through the day.","symptoms":["nausea","fatigue"],"feelings":"Tiredness can make you feel low. Resting is not laziness; it is what your body needs.","tips":["Avoid smoking and second-hand smoke.","Sip water regularly through the day."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms","lifestyle"],"sources":["unicef-t1","who-news","who-anc-sym"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby's brain and face are growing fast, and leg buds appear.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":{"kind":"image","alt":"Week 7 illustration","credit":"medicalgraphics","source_url":"https://www.medicalgraphics.de/en/product/embryo-7th-week-white/","axes":[{"id":"theme","source":"app"}],"renditions":[{"when":{"theme":"light"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-07.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":29546},{"when":{"theme":"dark"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-07-dark.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":42273}]},"sources":["mc1"]}},{"week":8,"title":"Your First Antenatal Visit","summary":"Nausea and tiredness often continue, and some women get headaches. Your first visit is a good time to ask about anything you are feeling.","symptoms":["nausea","fatigue","headaches"],"feelings":"Writing your questions down before the visit can ease worry.","tips":["Expect blood pressure, weight, urine and blood tests at your first visit.","Egypt's health units offer free screening for hepatitis B, HIV and syphilis."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["blood_pressure","urine_test","anaemia_test","infection_screening"],"topics":["visits","tests","symptoms"],"sources":["unicef-t1","who-news","eg-init-2025","eg-init-2024"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is just over 1 cm long, with a nose, upper lip and early fingers.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":13,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":{"kind":"image","alt":"Week 8 illustration","credit":"medicalgraphics","source_url":"https://www.medicalgraphics.de/en/product/embryo-8th-week-white/","axes":[{"id":"theme","source":"app"}],"renditions":[{"when":{"theme":"light"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-08.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":28876},{"when":{"theme":"dark"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-08-dark.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":43269}]},"sources":["mc1"]}},{"week":9,"title":"Protecting Your Energy","summary":"Tiredness and nausea are still common. Taking iron and folic acid every day helps protect you from anaemia, which can make tiredness worse.","symptoms":["fatigue","nausea"],"feelings":"If you feel overwhelmed, share it with your husband, family or doctor.","tips":["Take iron and folic acid as your doctor prescribes."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["supplements","symptoms"],"sources":["who-ifa","unicef-eg","unicef-t1"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is moving into the fetal stage, about 1.6 to 1.8 cm long, with visible toes and forming eyelids.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":17,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc1","cc"]}},{"week":10,"title":"Eating Well Despite Nausea","summary":"Constipation can start now, alongside nausea and tiredness. Water, fibre and regular meals all help.","symptoms":["constipation","nausea","fatigue"],"feelings":"On days when nausea stops you eating much, do what you can and keep sipping fluids.","tips":["Include iron-rich foods such as lentils, beans, leafy greens, eggs and meat.","Add fibre from vegetables, fruit, nuts and whole grains."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["nutrition","symptoms"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","who-news"],"baby":{"fact":"Fingers and toes are now separate, and tiny nails are starting to grow.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":{"kind":"image","alt":"Week 10 illustration","credit":"medicalgraphics","source_url":"https://www.medicalgraphics.de/en/product/fetus-10th-week-white/","axes":[{"id":"theme","source":"app"}],"renditions":[{"when":{"theme":"light"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-10.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":30420},{"when":{"theme":"dark"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-10-dark.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":43973}]},"sources":["cc"]}},{"week":11,"title":"Headaches and Bathroom Trips","summary":"You may still need to pass urine often, and headaches are common in early pregnancy. For many women, nausea starts to ease after week 12.","symptoms":["frequent_urination","headaches","nausea"],"feelings":"Worrying about your baby's health is natural, and your antenatal visits are there to answer your questions.","tips":["Ask your doctor before taking any medicine, including pain relief."],"danger_signs":["bleeding","leaking_fluid","severe_abdominal_pain"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms"],"sources":["unicef-t1","cc","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby can now open and close their fists and mouth, and bones are beginning to harden.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["cc"]}},{"week":12,"title":"Nausea Often Starts to Ease","summary":"Nausea often begins to ease from now on, though it lasts longer for some women. It usually settles by the second half of pregnancy.","symptoms":["nausea","fatigue"],"feelings":"Many women feel relief as the first trimester ends.","tips":["Your first antenatal contact is due by now. Tell your doctor how you have been feeling, including your mood."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["early_ultrasound"],"topics":["visits","symptoms"],"sources":["who-nv","mc-2t","who-anc","who-us","eg-pol","mc-dep"],"baby":{"fact":"All the main organs, limbs and muscles are in place, and your baby is about the size of a plum.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":"a plum"},"media":{"kind":"image","alt":"Week 12 illustration","credit":"medicalgraphics","source_url":"https://www.medicalgraphics.de/en/product/fetus-12th-week-white/","axes":[{"id":"theme","source":"app"}],"renditions":[{"when":{"theme":"light"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-12.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":30795},{"when":{"theme":"dark"},"url":"https://cdn.balsm.health/content/pregnancy/week-12-dark.jpg","mime":"image/jpeg","width":679,"height":480,"bytes":40944}]},"sources":["cc","mc1"]}},{"week":13,"title":"Energy Coming Back","summary":"Many women feel more energetic as the second trimester begins. Constipation may continue, so keep up water and fibre.","symptoms":["constipation"],"feelings":"A renewed sense of well-being is common now.","tips":["Ask about tetanus vaccination at your visit; Egypt's health units offer it based on past doses."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["tetanus_vaccine"],"topics":["vaccines","symptoms"],"sources":["mc-2t","who-anc-sym","eg-mohp-tt","eg-init-2025"],"baby":{"fact":"Bones in the skull and long bones of the arms and legs are hardening, and the vocal cords are forming.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2","cc"]}},{"week":14,"title":"Feeling More Like Yourself","summary":"Your appetite may return and your belly may begin to show. This is a good time to build a gentle activity routine.","symptoms":[],"feelings":"You may feel more up to preparing for your baby.","tips":["If your doctor agrees, aim for about 150 minutes of moderate activity a week, such as brisk walking."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["activity"],"sources":["mc-2t","who-pa","who-anc"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is about 8.7 cm from head to bottom and weighs around 45 g.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":87,"weight_g":45,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":15,"title":"Heartburn May Appear","summary":"Heartburn and constipation are common in the middle months. Small changes in how you eat can make a big difference.","symptoms":["heartburn","constipation"],"feelings":"Enjoy the easier days, and keep a note of symptoms to mention at your next visit.","tips":["Eat smaller meals and avoid lying down right after eating."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms","nutrition"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","mc-2t"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is growing quickly, and the scalp hair pattern is forming.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":16,"title":"A Growing Bump","summary":"Your belly is growing and your breasts may be larger. Some women start to feel aches in the back or pelvis.","symptoms":["back_pain"],"feelings":"Changes in your body shape can bring mixed feelings, and that is normal.","tips":["Include calcium-rich foods such as milk, yoghurt and cheese, and ask your doctor if you need a calcium supplement."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["nutrition","symptoms"],"sources":["mc-hp","who-ca","who-anc-sym"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is about 12 cm long and weighs around 110 g, and the eyes can move slowly.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":120,"weight_g":110,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2","cc"]}},{"week":17,"title":"Caring for Your Back","summary":"Back and pelvic aches are common as pregnancy progresses. Staying active is one of the best ways to prevent them.","symptoms":["back_pain","heartburn"],"feelings":"With more energy, this can be a good time to plan for the months ahead.","tips":["Keep up regular gentle exercise, such as walking."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["activity","symptoms"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","mc-2t"],"baby":{"fact":"Toenails are starting to grow, and your baby is rolling and flipping, though you may not feel it yet.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":18,"title":"Night-time Leg Cramps","summary":"Leg cramps, often at night, can start in the middle months. Stretching your calf before bed may help.","symptoms":["leg_cramps","back_pain"],"feelings":"Waiting for scan results can be stressful; ask your doctor what each test is for.","tips":["WHO recommends at least one ultrasound before 24 weeks; ask your doctor about timing."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["ultrasound_before_24"],"topics":["tests","symptoms"],"sources":["mc-2t","who-anc-sym","who-us"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is about 14 cm long and weighs around 200 g, and may begin to hear sounds.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":140,"weight_g":200,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":19,"title":"Mild Swelling Can Be Normal","summary":"Some swelling of the feet and ankles is common, especially at the end of the day. Swelling of the face or hands is different and needs checking.","symptoms":["swelling","headaches"],"feelings":"Knowing the warning signs can help you feel calmer and more in control.","tips":["Raise your feet when resting."],"danger_signs":["severe_headache","blurred_vision","face_hand_swelling"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"A creamy coating called vernix now covers your baby's skin to protect it.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":20,"title":"Halfway and First Movements","summary":"You are halfway, and you may start to feel your baby's first gentle movements. Heartburn may continue.","symptoms":["heartburn"],"feelings":"Feeling your baby move for the first time is a special moment for many women.","tips":["Your second antenatal contact is around now, with blood pressure and growth checks."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["blood_pressure","fetal_growth_check"],"topics":["visits","movements"],"sources":["mc-hp","mc-2t","who-anc","who-anc-sym"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is about 16 cm long and weighs around 320 g.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":160,"weight_g":320,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":21,"title":"Managing Heartburn","summary":"Heartburn and constipation can be bothersome now. Diet and lifestyle changes come first, and your doctor can suggest an antacid if needed.","symptoms":["heartburn","constipation","back_pain"],"feelings":"If discomfort is getting you down, mention it at your visit; there are safe options.","tips":["Do not take any medicine for heartburn without asking your doctor."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms"],"sources":["who-anc-sym"],"baby":{"fact":"Fine hair called lanugo covers your baby, and the sucking reflex is developing.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":22,"title":"Easing Leg Cramps","summary":"Leg cramps and back aches are common. Stretching, massage and warmth can bring relief.","symptoms":["leg_cramps","back_pain"],"feelings":"Poor sleep from cramps can affect your mood, so rest during the day when you can.","tips":["If cramps continue, ask your doctor whether magnesium or calcium is right for you."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","mc-2t"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is about 19 cm long, weighs around 460 g, and has visible eyebrows and hair.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":190,"weight_g":460,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":23,"title":"Preparing for the Sugar Test","summary":"Swollen feet and back aches are common now. Between weeks 24 and 28, your doctor will likely check you for pregnancy diabetes.","symptoms":["swelling","back_pain"],"feelings":"It is normal to feel nervous about tests; ask your doctor what to expect.","tips":["Ask your doctor how to prepare for the sugar test."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["tests"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","eg-gdm"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby's lungs are starting to make surfactant, which helps them inflate after birth, and fingerprint ridges are forming.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":24,"title":"Practice Tightenings May Start","summary":"You may notice your belly tightening now and then; these practice contractions are usually painless and irregular. Most women feel their baby move by now.","symptoms":["braxton_hicks","back_pain"],"feelings":"If you have not felt movements yet, telling your doctor can put your mind at ease.","tips":["Your pregnancy diabetes test is usually done between weeks 24 and 28."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["gdm_screening"],"topics":["tests","movements","symptoms"],"sources":["nhs-mov-wuth","nhs-mov-abb","eg-gdm"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is about 21 cm long and weighs over 600 g; the skin is still wrinkled and thin.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":210,"weight_g":630,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":25,"title":"Sleep Gets Harder","summary":"As your belly grows, finding a comfortable sleeping position can be harder. Heartburn at night may add to it.","symptoms":["sleep_trouble","heartburn"],"feelings":"Talking or singing to your baby can be a calming routine.","tips":["Keep taking iron and folic acid as your doctor advises."],"danger_signs":["fever","leaking_fluid"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["rest","supplements"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","who-ifa","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby may move in response to familiar sounds, such as your voice.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":26,"title":"Third Antenatal Contact","summary":"Back aches and tiredness may return as your pregnancy advances. Your third antenatal contact is due around now.","symptoms":["back_pain","fatigue"],"feelings":"Thinking about labour and becoming a mother can bring worry; learning what to expect helps.","tips":["Your doctor will check your blood pressure, urine and your baby's growth."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["blood_pressure","urine_test","fetal_growth_check"],"topics":["visits"],"sources":["mc-2t","who-anc"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is about 23 cm long, weighs nearly 820 g, and now has eyebrows and eyelashes.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":230,"weight_g":820,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":27,"title":"Getting Ready for the Last Stretch","summary":"Breathlessness and leg cramps can appear as the second trimester ends. Gentle activity and rest both help.","symptoms":["shortness_of_breath","leg_cramps"],"feelings":"Childbirth classes or reading about labour can make the unknown feel less scary.","tips":["Keep up gentle activity and rest when tired."],"danger_signs":["severe_headache","blurred_vision","face_hand_swelling"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["activity","birth_prep"],"sources":["mc-2t","mc3s","who-pa","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby's nervous system is maturing, and added fat is making the skin smoother.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc2"]}},{"week":28,"title":"Third Trimester Begins","summary":"Backaches, heartburn and tiredness are common in the last three months. From now on, get to know your baby's usual pattern of movements.","symptoms":["back_pain","heartburn","fatigue"],"feelings":"The last trimester can be physically and emotionally demanding, so accept help at home.","tips":["Contact your doctor straight away if movements slow down, change or stop."],"danger_signs":["reduced_movement"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["movements","symptoms"],"sources":["mc3s","nhs-mov-wuth","nhs-mov-abb","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby's eyelids can partly open, and they weigh about 1 kg.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":1000,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":29,"title":"Feeling Short of Breath","summary":"Feeling short of breath is common in the third trimester. Slowing down and sitting up straight can help.","symptoms":["shortness_of_breath","fatigue"],"feelings":"It is fine to slow down and say no to extra tasks.","tips":["Keep eating iron-rich meals."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms","nutrition"],"sources":["mc3s","who-anc-sym"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby can kick, stretch and make grasping movements, and you may feel them as firm pokes.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3","cc"]}},{"week":30,"title":"Fourth Antenatal Contact","summary":"Swollen feet and backache are common now. Your fourth antenatal contact is around this week.","symptoms":["swelling","back_pain"],"feelings":"Share any worries about the birth with your doctor; no question is too small.","tips":["Your doctor will check your blood pressure and your baby's growth and position."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["blood_pressure","fetal_growth_check","fetal_position_check"],"topics":["visits"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","mc-hp","who-anc"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby can open their eyes wide, may have a good head of hair, and weighs about 1.3 kg.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":1300,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":31,"title":"Bathroom Trips Return","summary":"Needing to pass urine often may return as pregnancy advances. Practice tightenings may also become more noticeable.","symptoms":["frequent_urination","braxton_hicks","swelling"],"feelings":"Feeling impatient or uncomfortable is common at this stage.","tips":["Raise your legs when sitting to ease swelling."],"danger_signs":["severe_headache","face_hand_swelling"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["symptoms"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","unicef-t1","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"Most major development is complete, and your baby now gains weight quickly.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":32,"title":"Restless Nights","summary":"Sleep may be harder with a bigger belly, leg cramps and night-time trips to the bathroom. Short daytime rests can help.","symptoms":["sleep_trouble","leg_cramps","frequent_urination"],"feelings":"Tiredness can make worries feel bigger; talk them through with someone you trust.","tips":["Keep noticing your baby's movements every day."],"danger_signs":["bleeding","leaking_fluid","severe_abdominal_pain"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["rest","movements"],"sources":["who-anc-sym","nhs-mov-wuth","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby weighs about 1.7 kg, toenails are visible and the soft lanugo hair starts to shed.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":1700,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":33,"title":"Planning for the Birth","summary":"Breathlessness and backache may continue. This is a good time to decide where you will give birth and how you will get there.","symptoms":["shortness_of_breath","back_pain"],"feelings":"Having a plan often eases anxiety about labour.","tips":["Discuss your birth plan with your doctor."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["birth_prep"],"sources":["mc3s","who-anc-sym"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby's pupils can now respond to light, and the bones are hardening while the skull stays soft.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":34,"title":"Fifth Antenatal Contact","summary":"Practice tightenings and frequent urination are common. Your fifth antenatal contact is due around now.","symptoms":["braxton_hicks","frequent_urination"],"feelings":"As the birth gets closer, excitement and nerves often grow together.","tips":["Your doctor will check your blood pressure, urine and your baby's position."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["blood_pressure","urine_test","fetal_position_check"],"topics":["visits"],"sources":["who-anc","unicef-t1"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby weighs about 2.1 kg, and the fingernails now reach the fingertips.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":2100,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":35,"title":"Feeling Heavy and Slow","summary":"You may feel heavy and tire quickly, with backache and poor sleep. Your baby should keep moving regularly until birth.","symptoms":["back_pain","sleep_trouble","fatigue"],"feelings":"It is fine to ask family to help with daily tasks.","tips":["Contact your doctor straight away if movements slow down or change."],"danger_signs":["reduced_movement"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["movements","rest"],"sources":["mc3s","nhs-mov-wuth"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby now fills most of the womb and has less room, but you should still feel regular rolls and stretches.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":36,"title":"Sixth Antenatal Contact","summary":"Many babies settle head down by now. You may feel more pressure low in your belly and need to pass urine more often.","symptoms":["frequent_urination","back_pain"],"feelings":"Getting ready for your baby can be both exciting and tiring.","tips":["Your doctor will check your baby's position at this visit."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":["fetal_position_check"],"topics":["visits"],"sources":["cc","who-anc","unicef-t1"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby's skin is getting smoother and limbs chubbier, and most babies are head down by now.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3","cc"]}},{"week":37,"title":"Know the Signs of Labour","summary":"Practice tightenings may come more often now. Real labour brings contractions that become regular and stronger.","symptoms":["braxton_hicks","swelling"],"feelings":"Feeling ready one day and scared the next is common.","tips":["Keep your hospital bag ready.","Contact your doctor if your waters break, you have bleeding, or movements decrease."],"danger_signs":["bleeding","reduced_movement","leaking_fluid"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["birth_prep"],"sources":["mc3","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is now considered early term, can grasp firmly, and the head may move down into your pelvis.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":38,"title":"Waiting Can Be Hard","summary":"Discomfort, poor sleep and impatience are common in the final weeks. Your seventh antenatal contact is due around now.","symptoms":["sleep_trouble","back_pain","mood_changes"],"feelings":"Impatience is natural; try to rest and keep plans simple.","tips":["Ask your doctor any questions about labour and birth."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["visits","birth_prep"],"sources":["mc3s","who-anc","mc-hp"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby may weigh about 2.9 kg, though healthy sizes vary widely, and most of the lanugo is gone.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":2900,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":39,"title":"Full Term","summary":"Your pregnancy is now full term. Rest as much as you can and keep track of your baby's movements.","symptoms":["fatigue","frequent_urination"],"feelings":"Every pregnancy ends in its own time; try not to compare yourself with others.","tips":["Contact your doctor if your waters break, or you have bleeding, fever or severe abdominal pain."],"danger_signs":["bleeding","fever","leaking_fluid","severe_abdominal_pain"],"tests_due":[],"topics":["birth_prep","rest","movements"],"sources":["mc3","who-ds"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby is now full term and is adding fat all over to stay warm after birth.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":null,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3"]}},{"week":40,"title":"Your Due Date","summary":"A due date is only an estimate, and many babies arrive before or after it. Your eighth antenatal contact is due now.","symptoms":["mood_changes","fatigue"],"feelings":"Passing your due date can be frustrating; your doctor will explain the plan if labour has not started.","tips":["Follow your doctor's plan if labour has not started."],"danger_signs":[],"tests_due":[],"topics":["visits","birth_prep"],"sources":["cc","who-anc"],"baby":{"fact":"Your baby may weigh about 3.4 kg, but healthy babies come in many sizes.","fetal_size":{"length_mm":null,"weight_g":3400,"comparison":null},"media":null,"sources":["mc3","cc"]}}]}''',
